From 14b82eeaa33ccf0d20dc450675de39c741923884 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nunogt <nunogt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 19:16:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Defer beacon set in hostapd_reload_bss() until interface
 is enabled

hostapd_reload_bss() calls ieee802_11_set_beacon() unconditionally, guarded
only by hapd->started. hapd->started is set in hostapd_setup_bss() during
interface bring-up, before channel selection (ACS) or DFS CAC completes. If a
configuration reload occurs while the interface is still in HAPD_IFACE_ACS (or
HAPD_IFACE_DFS), the BSS has started == 1 but iface->state != HAPD_IFACE_ENABLED,
i.e. there is no valid operating channel yet.

ieee802_11_set_beacon() -> __ieee802_11_set_beacon() does not check the
interface state (only !drv_priv and csa_in_progress), so it proceeds to
hostapd_drv_set_ap() and the driver rejects the request with "Failed to set
beacon parameters". The new Beacon -- which, with IEEE 802.11r enabled, carries
the Mobility Domain element -- is never installed, and the interface keeps
radiating the previous Beacon (without the MDE). With multiple radios the
failure is non-deterministic: whichever radio is still completing ACS when the
cross-interface beacon refresh runs is the one that fails.

Defer the beacon update until the interface reaches HAPD_IFACE_ENABLED,
mirroring the guard already used for the OWE transition beacon update. When
ACS/DFS completes, hostapd_setup_interface_complete_sync() installs the Beacon
via ieee802_11_set_beacons(), so the deferred update is not lost.

Signed-off-by: YOUR NAME <YOUR EMAIL>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
index 7d924893f..19470cf64 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -186,7 +186,19 @@ static void hostapd_reload_bss(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
 
 	hostapd_neighbor_sync_own_report(hapd);
 
-	ieee802_11_set_beacon(hapd);
+	/*
+	 * Do not push a new Beacon while the interface has not finished coming
+	 * up (e.g., ACS or DFS CAC still in progress on a configuration reload).
+	 * hapd->started is set during bring-up before channel selection
+	 * completes, so it is not sufficient on its own: with started == 1 but
+	 * iface->state != HAPD_IFACE_ENABLED there is no valid operating channel
+	 * and the driver rejects set_ap ("Failed to set beacon parameters"),
+	 * dropping the new Beacon (which, with IEEE 802.11r, carries the
+	 * Mobility Domain element). The Beacon is installed once the interface
+	 * reaches HAPD_IFACE_ENABLED.
+	 */
+	if (hapd->iface->state == HAPD_IFACE_ENABLED)
+		ieee802_11_set_beacon(hapd);
 	hostapd_update_wps(hapd);
 
 	if (hapd->conf->ssid.ssid_set &&
